Teach configure about dl_iterate_phdr on NetBSD.

`unwind-dw2-fde-dip.c` only uses `PT_GNU_EH_FRAME` -- the path that finds
unwind tables through the dynamic loader -- when three things hold:

    #if !defined(inhibit_libc) && defined(HAVE_LD_EH_FRAME_HDR) \
        && defined(TARGET_DL_ITERATE_PHDR) \
        && (defined(__OpenBSD__) || defined(__NetBSD__))

The guard names NetBSD, but `TARGET_DL_ITERATE_PHDR` can never be defined for
it: the case that sets `gcc_cv_target_dl_iterate_phdr` covers only solaris2,
dragonfly/freebsd and linux-musl, so NetBSD falls through as "unknown".

    checking dl_iterate_phdr in target C library... unknown

Without it the unwinder has no `dl_iterate_phdr` path and falls back to
registered frames alone, so a C++ throw finds no handler and aborts.

NetBSD has provided `dl_iterate_phdr` since 5.0, declared in `<link_elf.h>`, so
answer yes for it directly, as solaris2 and linux-musl already do. Probing the
header the way the freebsd arm does is not an option here: `target_header_dir`
is empty in a compiler configured `--without-headers`, so the grep cannot
succeed and the probe records "no" -- the same "cannot reach it, so record
absent" failure this patch exists to fix.

Both `configure.ac` and the generated `configure` are patched, since the build
uses the shipped script rather than regenerating it.

--- a/gcc/configure.ac
+++ b/gcc/configure.ac
@@ -7143,6 +7143,9 @@
       gcc_cv_target_dl_iterate_phdr=no
     fi
     ;;
+  *-*-netbsd*)
+    gcc_cv_target_dl_iterate_phdr=yes
+    ;;
   *-linux-musl*)
     gcc_cv_target_dl_iterate_phdr=yes
     ;;
--- a/gcc/configure
+++ b/gcc/configure
@@ -33645,6 +33645,9 @@
       gcc_cv_target_dl_iterate_phdr=no
     fi
     ;;
+  *-*-netbsd*)
+    gcc_cv_target_dl_iterate_phdr=yes
+    ;;
   *-linux-musl*)
     gcc_cv_target_dl_iterate_phdr=yes
     ;;
